<section class="studio-panel"><h2>A useful drafting prompt</h2><p>Start with: “Help me outline an article for [audience] about [question]. Use only the experience and evidence below. Separate observations from assumptions, mark claims to verify, and end with a practical next step.”</p><p>Add your own observations, then check original sources, dates, quotations, permissions and the final meaning. AI does not replace research or your judgement.</p><h2>Write from your phone</h2><ol><li>Bookmark this Studio. On iPhone use Safari → Share → Add to Home Screen; on Android use your browser menu → Add to Home screen if offered.</li><li>Capture an idea and save it. Continue in the editor; autosave starts after the first save.</li><li>Use Media to upload a photograph or video from your phone. Record permission and add meaningful alternative text.</li><li>Preview the draft, check facts and links, then explicitly publish or schedule.</li><li>Prepare separate social drafts. Connections shows which accounts and permissions are confirmed. Some formats require you to finish in the platform’s own app.</li></ol><p><a href="<?=url('/write/releases')?>">Consent records</a> · <a href="<?=url('/write/newsletter')?>">Newsletter</a> · <a href="<?=url('/write/discovery')?>">Search performance</a> · <a href="<?=url('/write/account')?>">Change password</a></p></section>
